# DTF tier manifest: storage-integrity-serve-routes  (artifact-keeper#4323)
# Profile-set: filesystem / single. Sibling of storage-integrity (#3919, which
# covers the generic download route). The oracle damages stored objects on the
# backend's /data volume (a throwaway postgres:16-alpine container with
# --volumes-from the backend; the backend image has no shell) and asserts that
# the other serve paths fail closed:
#
#   #4323  a small corrupted object answers 502 {"code":"STORED_OBJECT_INTEGRITY"}
#          with none of its bytes on the generic download route, on a
#          format-native route (Terraform module archive, served through the
#          shared hosted fetch) and through a virtual repository (generic),
#          where the 502 is final: the walk does not fall through to the
#          second member's bytes for the same path. A corrupted object above
#          the 4 MiB pre-check limit is never delivered complete on the
#          format route.
#          RED on ak-backend:1.11.5: the generic route answers 200 and aborts
#          the body; the format route and the virtual answer 200 with the
#          corrupted bytes, complete.
#   #4323  OCI blob pulls (GET /v2/<repo>/<image>/blobs/<digest>) verify the
#          stored bytes against the digest: a corrupted 300 KB layer is
#          answered 502 with the OCI error code STORED_OBJECT_INTEGRITY and
#          none of its bytes (larger layers are cut short before their end).
#          RED on ak-backend:1.11.5: the corrupted layer is served complete.
#   Controls: intact objects download byte-identical on every route; a
#          proper sub-range of a corrupted object is still served.
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: ~40 calls back to back.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
